1
00:00:01,198 --> 00:00:06,000
One evening, a few days after the writing had appeared in Charlotte's Web,

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,639
the spider called a meeting of all the animals in the barn cellar. I shall

3
00:00:10,639 --> 00:00:21,599
begin by calling the roll. Wilbur here, said the pig. Gander here, said the gender.

4
00:00:21,599 --> 00:00:27,840
You sound like three ganders, muttered Charlotte. Why can't you just say here?

5
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:30,158
Why do you have to repeat everything?

6
00:00:30,158 --> 00:00:36,880
It's my idio idiosyncrasy, replied the gender. Goose, said Charlotte. Here,

7
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:45,599
here, said the goose. Charlotte glared at her. Goslings 1 through 7.

8
00:00:45,599 --> 00:00:48,719
Said the gozlings.

9
00:00:48,719 --> 00:00:53,599
This is getting to be quite a meeting, said Charlotte. Anybody would think we

10
00:00:53,599 --> 00:00:58,238
had three ganders, three geese, and 21 goings.

11
00:00:58,238 --> 00:01:08,238
Sheep, answered the sheep all together. Lambs, answered the lambs all together.

12
00:01:08,238 --> 00:01:16,079
Templeton, no answer. Templeton, no answer.

13
00:01:16,079 --> 00:01:21,118
Well, we are all here except the rat, said Charlotte. I guess we can proceed

14
00:01:21,118 --> 00:01:26,079
without him. Now, all of you must have noticed what's been going on around here

15
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:31,599
the last few days. The message I wrote in my web praising Wilbur has been

16
00:01:31,599 --> 00:01:37,039
received. The Zuckermanmans have fallen for it, and so has everybody else.

17
00:01:37,039 --> 00:01:42,158
Zuckerman thinks Wilbur is an unusual pig, and therefore he won't want to kill

18
00:01:42,158 --> 00:01:50,319
him and eat him. I dare say my trick will work, and Wilbur's life can be saved. Hooray!

19
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:53,359
cried everybody.

20
00:01:53,359 --> 00:01:56,319
Thank you very much, said Charlotte.

21
00:01:56,319 --> 00:02:01,920
Now, I called this meeting in order to get suggestions. I need new ideas for

22
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:09,279
the web. People are already getting sick of reading the words some pig.

23
00:02:09,279 --> 00:02:14,158
If anybody can think of another message or remark, I'll be glad to weave it into

24
00:02:14,158 --> 00:02:21,760
the web. Any suggestions for a new slogan? How about pig supreme? asked one

25
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:25,520
of the lambs. No good, said Charlotte.

26
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:32,079
It sounds like a rich dessert. How about terrific, terrific, terrific, asked the

27
00:02:32,079 --> 00:02:38,479
goose. Cut that down to one terrific, and it will do very nicely, said

28
00:02:38,479 --> 00:02:44,800
Charlotte. I think terrific might impress Zuckerman.

29
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:51,279
But Charlotte, said Wilbur, I'm not terrific. That doesn't make a particle

30
00:02:51,279 --> 00:02:57,520
of difference, replied Charlotte. Not a particle. People believe almost anything

31
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:04,158
they see in print. Does anybody here know how to spell terrific? I think,

32
00:03:04,158 --> 00:03:17,560
said the gander. It's T E R I F I D C C.

33
00:03:18,639 --> 00:03:24,399
What kind of an acrobat do you think I am? said Charlotte in disgust. I would

34
00:03:24,399 --> 00:03:29,279
have to have St. Vitis's dance to weave a word like that into my web. Sorry,

35
00:03:29,279 --> 00:03:37,279
sorry, sorry, said the gander. Then the oldest sheep spoke up. I agree that

36
00:03:37,279 --> 00:03:44,319
there should be something new written in the web if Wilbur's life is to be saved.

37
00:03:44,319 --> 00:03:53,359
And if Charlotte needs help in finding words, I think she can get it from our friend Templeton.

38
00:03:53,359 --> 00:04:00,319
The rat visits the dump regularly and has access to old magazines. He can tear

39
00:04:00,319 --> 00:04:05,198
out bits of advertisements and bring them up here to the barn cellar so that

40
00:04:05,198 --> 00:04:08,000
Charlotte can have something to copy.

41
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:14,880
Good idea, said Charlotte. But I'm not sure Templeton will be willing to help.

42
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:22,399
You know how he is, always looking out for himself, never thinking of the other fellow.

43
00:04:22,399 --> 00:04:29,439
I bet I can get him to help, said the old sheep. I'll appeal to his baser

44
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:36,880
instincts, of which he has plenty. Here he comes now. Everybody, keep quiet

45
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:42,079
while I put the matter up to him. The rat entered the barn the way he always

46
00:04:42,079 --> 00:04:45,520
did, creeping along close to the wall.

47
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:52,238
"What's up?" he asked, seeing the animals assembled. "We're holding a

48
00:04:52,238 --> 00:04:57,439
director's meeting," replied the old sheep.

49
00:04:57,439 --> 00:05:03,679
Well, break it up, said Templeton. Means bore me. And the rat began to climb a

50
00:05:03,679 --> 00:05:10,639
rope that hung against the wall. Look, said the old sheep. Next time you go to

51
00:05:10,639 --> 00:05:16,319
the dump, Templeton, bring back a clipping from a magazine. Charlotte

52
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:21,520
needs new ideas so she can write messages in her web and save Wilbur's

53
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:28,399
life. Let him die, said the rat. I should worry.

54
00:05:28,399 --> 00:05:35,118
You'll worry all right when next winter comes, said the sheep. You'll worry all

55
00:05:35,118 --> 00:05:41,359
right on a zero morning next January when Wilbur is dead and nobody comes

56
00:05:41,359 --> 00:05:47,279
down here with a nice pale of warm slops to pour into the trough. Wilbur's

57
00:05:47,279 --> 00:05:55,198
leftover food is your chief source of supply, Templeton. You know that

58
00:05:55,198 --> 00:06:02,399
Wilbur's food is your food. Therefore, Wilbur's destiny and your destiny are

59
00:06:02,399 --> 00:06:08,479
closely linked. If Wilbur's killed and his trough stands empty day after day,

60
00:06:08,479 --> 00:06:16,399
you'll grow so thin we can look right through your stomach and see objects on the other side.

61
00:06:16,399 --> 00:06:22,560
Templeton's whiskers quivered. Maybe you're right," he said gruffly. "I'm

62
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:27,039
making a trip to the dump tomorrow afternoon. I'll bring back a magazine

63
00:06:27,039 --> 00:06:33,039
clipping if I can find one." "Thanks," said Charlotte. "The meeting is now

64
00:06:33,039 --> 00:06:38,639
adjourned. I have a busy evening ahead of me. I've got to tear my web apart and

65
00:06:38,639 --> 00:06:41,599
write terrific."

66
00:06:41,599 --> 00:06:48,079
Wilbur blushed. But I'm not terrific, Charlotte. I'm just about average for a

67
00:06:48,079 --> 00:06:54,079
pig. You're terrific as far as I'm concerned, replied Charlotte sweetly.

68
00:06:54,079 --> 00:07:00,880
And that's what counts. You're my best friend, and I think you're sensational.

69
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:06,000
Now, stop arguing and go get some sleep.
